--- body ---
## Context

Panel A of `fig_exp2_arms_comparison` currently shows only `inventory_rows`
(a count of all rows in the output table, used as a coverage proxy). This
hides a key signal: some of those rows are hallucinated plants (FP).

The figure should distinguish:
- Correctly identified plants (TP) — matched against the 163-plant reference
- Hallucinated plants (FP) — rows in the output not matched to any reference plant

This mirrors the visual language of `fig_direct_p1_base` (the method convergence
strip plot) where blue=TP and orange=FP are shown together.

## Design

**Diverging bar chart**: TP bars extend upward from zero (blue, `COLOR_MATCHED`);
FP bars extend downward below zero (orange, `COLOR_HALLUC`). Zero baseline is
a horizontal line. This makes recall and hallucination rate immediately readable
without mental arithmetic — tall blue bar + shallow orange bar = good run.

In `plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py`:
- Replace the single `inventory_rows` bar with two series:
  - `n_matched` plotted as positive bars (upward, blue)
  - `n_hallucinated` (= `inventory_rows - n_matched`) plotted as negative bars
    (downward, orange) via `ax.bar(..., -n_hallucinated, ...)`
- Use the same colour constants (`COLOR_MATCHED`, `COLOR_HALLUC`) as the
  method-convergence figure
- Y-axis label: "Plants" with tick labels showing absolute values on both sides
- Data source: `tab_exp2_arms_runs_view.csv` must carry `n_matched`; confirm
  or patch the mart VIEW to include it

Panel B (report length) and Panel C (cost) are unchanged.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Panel A shows TP and FP separately, same colour scheme as fig_direct_p1_base
- [ ] `tab_exp2_arms_runs_view.csv` carries the needed columns (or mart patched)
- [ ] Figure regenerates cleanly on clean data (after 0313)
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
